					"numinlets" : 1,
					"numoutlets" : 0,
					"patching_rect" : [ 31.0, 196.0, 484.0, 121.0 ],
					"text" : "Unpacks leftmost value is 0 for solo layers and 1 for regular layers. This can be used to control low/high pass filter to simulate subs vs regular speakers. To specify the crossover frequency use the D4-binaural-xover-frequency send. To specify sub channel gain use the D4-binaural-sub-gain (e.g. to be used with headphones that are not as good at reproducing lows). Use D4-binaural-disable-highpass send to toggle highpass frequency filtering on regular speakes (enabled by default, or 0). You can also do this by passing the second argument to the patch (0 to keep it enabled or 1 to disable it). Receives for these sends are located in the blue \"p filtering\" patcher below."
				}

			}
